    <xsd:complexType name="cellPositioningChordwiseType">
        <xsd:annotation>
            <xsd:appinfo>
                <sd:schemaDoc>
                    <ddue:summary>
                        <ddue:para>Border of a cell at its leading or trailing edge</ddue:para>
                    </ddue:summary>
                    <ddue:remarks>
                        <ddue:content>
                            <ddue:para>The border is given in one of three ways:</ddue:para>
                            <ddue:list class="bullet">
                                <ddue:listItem>
                                    <ddue:para>
                                        <ddue:codeInline>xsi1</ddue:codeInline> and <ddue:codeInline>xsi2</ddue:codeInline>: the relative chordwise position of the border at the inner and at the outer end of the cell, so that the border may run at an angle to the lines of constant ξ;</ddue:para>
                                </ddue:listItem>
                                <ddue:listItem>
                                    <ddue:para>
                                        <ddue:codeInline>sparUID</ddue:codeInline>: the border follows that spar;</ddue:para>
                                </ddue:listItem>
                                <ddue:listItem>
                                    <ddue:para>
                                        <ddue:codeInline>contourCoordinate</ddue:codeInline>: the border follows the skin at that position, from 0 at the leading edge to 1 at the trailing edge.</ddue:para>
                                </ddue:listItem>
                            </ddue:list>
                            <ddue:para>A contour coordinate runs on the skin itself, not on the chord surface: it is the relative position along the surface, so a border given this way follows the skin. Because the two kinds of border are of a different nature, either all four borders of a cell are given as contour coordinates or none of them is.</ddue:para>
                        </ddue:content>
                    </ddue:remarks>
                </sd:schemaDoc>
            </xsd:appinfo>
        </xsd:annotation>
        <xsd:complexContent>
            <xsd:extension base="complexBaseType">
                <xsd:choice>
                    <xsd:sequence>
                        <xsd:element name="xsi1" type="doubleBaseType">
                            <xsd:annotation>
                                <xsd:documentation>Relative chordwise position of the border at the inner end</xsd:documentation>
                            </xsd:annotation>
                        </xsd:element>
                        <xsd:element name="xsi2" type="doubleBaseType">
                            <xsd:annotation>
                                <xsd:documentation>Relative chordwise position of the border at the outer end</xsd:documentation>
                            </xsd:annotation>
                        </xsd:element>
                    </xsd:sequence>
                    <xsd:element name="sparUID" type="stringUIDBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>UID of the spar the border follows</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="contourCoordinate" type="doubleBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>Position of the border on the skin, from 0 at the leading edge to 1 at the trailing edge</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                </xsd:choice>
            </xsd:extension>
        </xsd:complexContent>
    </xsd:complexType>

    <xsd:complexType name="cellPositioningSpanwiseType">
        <xsd:annotation>
            <xsd:appinfo>
                <sd:schemaDoc>
                    <ddue:summary>
                        <ddue:para>Border of a cell at its inner or outer end</ddue:para>
                    </ddue:summary>
                    <ddue:remarks>
                        <ddue:content>
                            <ddue:para>The border is given in one of three ways:</ddue:para>
                            <ddue:list class="bullet">
                                <ddue:listItem>
                                    <ddue:para>
                                        <ddue:codeInline>eta1</ddue:codeInline> and <ddue:codeInline>eta2</ddue:codeInline>: the relative spanwise position of the border at the leading and at the trailing edge of the cell, so that the border may run at an angle to the lines of constant η;</ddue:para>
                                </ddue:listItem>
                                <ddue:listItem>
                                    <ddue:para>
                                        <ddue:codeInline>ribDefinitionUID</ddue:codeInline> with <ddue:codeInline>ribNumber</ddue:codeInline>: the border follows that rib of that rib set;</ddue:para>
                                </ddue:listItem>
                                <ddue:listItem>
                                    <ddue:para>
                                        <ddue:codeInline>contourCoordinate</ddue:codeInline>: the border follows the skin at that position, from 0 at the root to 1 at the tip.</ddue:para>
                                </ddue:listItem>
                            </ddue:list>
                            <ddue:para>A contour coordinate runs on the skin itself, not on the chord surface: it is the relative position along the surface, so a border given this way follows the skin. Because the two kinds of border are of a different nature, either all four borders of a cell are given as contour coordinates or none of them is.</ddue:para>
                        </ddue:content>
                    </ddue:remarks>
                </sd:schemaDoc>
            </xsd:appinfo>
        </xsd:annotation>
        <xsd:complexContent>
            <xsd:extension base="complexBaseType">
                <xsd:choice>
                    <xsd:sequence>
                        <xsd:element name="eta1" type="etaIsoLineType">
                            <xsd:annotation>
                                <xsd:documentation>Relative spanwise position of the border at the leading edge</xsd:documentation>
                            </xsd:annotation>
                        </xsd:element>
                        <xsd:element name="eta2" type="etaIsoLineType">
                            <xsd:annotation>
                                <xsd:documentation>Relative spanwise position of the border at the trailing edge</xsd:documentation>
                            </xsd:annotation>
                        </xsd:element>
                    </xsd:sequence>
                    <xsd:sequence>
                        <xsd:element name="ribNumber" type="integerBaseType">
                            <xsd:annotation>
                                <xsd:documentation>Number of the rib within its set</xsd:documentation>
                            </xsd:annotation>
                        </xsd:element>
                        <xsd:element name="ribDefinitionUID" type="stringUIDBaseType">
                            <xsd:annotation>
                                <xsd:documentation>UID of the rib or rib set the border follows</xsd:documentation>
                            </xsd:annotation>
                        </xsd:element>
                    </xsd:sequence>
                    <xsd:element name="contourCoordinate" type="doubleBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>Position of the border on the skin, from 0 at the root to 1 at the tip</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                </xsd:choice>
            </xsd:extension>
        </xsd:complexContent>
    </xsd:complexType>

