    <xsd:complexType name="etaIsoLineType">
        <xsd:annotation>
            <xsd:appinfo>
                <sd:schemaDoc>
                    <ddue:summary>
                        <ddue:para>Spanwise position, given as a relative coordinate</ddue:para>
                    </ddue:summary>
                    <ddue:remarks>
                        <ddue:content>
                            <ddue:para>A position along the span, given by the relative coordinate η (<ddue:codeInline>eta</ddue:codeInline>), which runs from 0 to 1. It describes the line of all points of the chord surface with this η.</ddue:para>
                            <ddue:para>The <ddue:codeInline>referenceUID</ddue:codeInline> selects the coordinates: it references either a segment of the wing, and the values are then the coordinates of that segment (<ddue:codeInline>wingSegmentType</ddue:codeInline>), or a component segment, and the values are then the coordinates of the component segment (<ddue:codeInline>componentSegmentType</ddue:codeInline>).</ddue:para>
                            <ddue:para>Where the element that uses this type says so, the <ddue:codeInline>referenceUID</ddue:codeInline> may also reference a curve, e.g. a spar; η is then measured along that curve (see <ddue:codeInline>wingSparType</ddue:codeInline>).</ddue:para>
                        </ddue:content>
                    </ddue:remarks>
                </sd:schemaDoc>
            </xsd:appinfo>
        </xsd:annotation>
        <xsd:complexContent>
            <xsd:extension base="complexBaseType">
                <xsd:all>
                    <xsd:element name="eta" type="doubleBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>Relative spanwise position</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="referenceUID" type="stringUIDBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>UID of the segment, component segment or curve along which the position is measured</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                </xsd:all>
            </xsd:extension>
        </xsd:complexContent>
    </xsd:complexType>

    <xsd:complexType name="etaXsiPointType">
        <xsd:annotation>
            <xsd:appinfo>
                <sd:schemaDoc>
                    <ddue:summary>
                        <ddue:para>Point on the chord surface, given in relative coordinates</ddue:para>
                    </ddue:summary>
                    <ddue:remarks>
                        <ddue:content>
                            <ddue:para>A point of the chord surface of the component segment, the surface spanned by the chord lines of its elements (see <ddue:codeInline>componentSegmentType</ddue:codeInline>), given by the relative spanwise coordinate η (<ddue:codeInline>eta</ddue:codeInline>) and the relative chordwise coordinate ξ (<ddue:codeInline>xsi</ddue:codeInline>). Both run from 0 to 1.</ddue:para>
                            <ddue:para>The <ddue:codeInline>referenceUID</ddue:codeInline> selects the coordinates: it references either a segment of the wing, and the values are then the coordinates of that segment (<ddue:codeInline>wingSegmentType</ddue:codeInline>), or a component segment, and the values are then the coordinates of the component segment (<ddue:codeInline>componentSegmentType</ddue:codeInline>).</ddue:para>
                            <ddue:para>In the coordinates of a component segment, η = 0 and η = 1 lie on its inner and its outer section element, ξ = 0 on the leading and ξ = 1 on the trailing edge.</ddue:para>
                        </ddue:content>
                    </ddue:remarks>
                </sd:schemaDoc>
            </xsd:appinfo>
        </xsd:annotation>
        <xsd:complexContent>
            <xsd:extension base="complexBaseType">
                <xsd:all>
                    <xsd:element name="eta" type="doubleBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>Relative spanwise position on the chord surface</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="xsi" type="doubleBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>Relative chordwise position on the chord surface</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="referenceUID" type="stringUIDBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>UID of the segment or component segment whose coordinates are used</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                </xsd:all>
            </xsd:extension>
        </xsd:complexContent>
    </xsd:complexType>

    <xsd:complexType name="etaXsiRelHeightPointType">
        <xsd:annotation>
            <xsd:appinfo>
                <sd:schemaDoc>
                    <ddue:summary>
                        <ddue:para>Point between the lower and the upper surface of the wing</ddue:para>
                    </ddue:summary>
                    <ddue:remarks>
                        <ddue:content>
                            <ddue:para>A point above or below the chord surface of the component segment, the surface spanned by the chord lines of its elements (see <ddue:codeInline>componentSegmentType</ddue:codeInline>): it lies on the normal of the chord surface through the point with the relative coordinates η (<ddue:codeInline>eta</ddue:codeInline>) and ξ (<ddue:codeInline>xsi</ddue:codeInline>).</ddue:para>
                            <ddue:para>
                                <ddue:codeInline>relHeight</ddue:codeInline> gives its position on that normal, relative to the thickness of the wing at this place: 0 is the point on the lower and 1 the point on the upper surface of the wing, and values in between are interpolated linearly. Without relHeight the point lies on the chord surface.</ddue:para>
                            <ddue:para>The <ddue:codeInline>referenceUID</ddue:codeInline> selects the coordinates: it references either a segment of the wing, and the values are then the coordinates of that segment (<ddue:codeInline>wingSegmentType</ddue:codeInline>), or a component segment, and the values are then the coordinates of the component segment (<ddue:codeInline>componentSegmentType</ddue:codeInline>).</ddue:para>
                        </ddue:content>
                    </ddue:remarks>
                </sd:schemaDoc>
            </xsd:appinfo>
        </xsd:annotation>
        <xsd:complexContent>
            <xsd:extension base="complexBaseType">
                <xsd:all>
                    <xsd:element name="eta" type="doubleBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>Relative spanwise position on the chord surface</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="xsi" type="doubleBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>Relative chordwise position on the chord surface</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="relHeight" minOccurs="0" type="doubleBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>Position on the normal of the chord surface, from 0 on the lower to 1 on the upper surface of the wing</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                    <xsd:element name="referenceUID" type="stringUIDBaseType">
                        <xsd:annotation>
                            <xsd:documentation>UID of the segment or component segment whose coordinates are used</xsd:documentation>
                        </xsd:annotation>
                    </xsd:element>
                </xsd:all>
            </xsd:extension>
        </xsd:complexContent>
    </xsd:complexType>

